  "conclusion": "The uniform two-convolution residual tree generalizes, but it is substantially underpowered. Test reduction rises from 13.67% at the root to 30.83% at depth two and only 33.17% at depth three. The three grandchildren yield just 3.97%, 1.06%, and 4.74% local test gains. Test is slightly better than train at every stage, so overfitting is not the explanation. The architectural bundle is 89.31% smaller per node than the superseded three-convolution tree, but because width and depth both changed this run does not isolate the causal effect of the residual addition itself."
